<annotations>
<annotation ref="figure" text="Five concentric circles are level curves of f, with values c 1, c star, c 3, c 4, c 5 increasing outward. A green parabola-shaped constraint curve, g of x y equals 0, opens downward and touches the circle f equals c star, drawn in red, at its highest point, labeled x star y star. At that point a red arrow, the gradient of f, points down and a green arrow, the gradient of g, points up: the two gradients are collinear. Two other marked points, x 1 y 1 and x 2 y 2, lie on the constraint curve on either side.">
  <annotation ref="lc-g" text="The constraint curve, where g of x y equals 0, drawn in green. It crosses the outer level curves of f and is tangent to the level curve f equals c star."/>
