<annotations>
<annotation ref="figure" text="A right triangle A B C with the right angle at C. The hypotenuse A B is horizontal, running from A on the left to B on the right. The altitude from C meets the hypotenuse at right angles at the point D, splitting it into a left piece of length a and a right piece of length b. The altitude itself has length h. The two small triangles A D C and D B C, shaded in different colors, are similar to the whole triangle and to each other, which forces a over h to equal h over b, so h is the square root of a b, the geometric mean of a and b.">
  <annotation ref="ga-triangle" text="The right triangle A B C, with the right angle at the top vertex C and the hypotenuse A B along the bottom."/>
